{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/planarity\/planarembedding"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A planar embedding of a graph: a rotation system, the clockwise order of the edges around each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex, over every edge position. Its faces satisfy Euler’s formula, n − m + f = 2, in every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connected component with an edge."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity"]]},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PlanarEmbedding"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A self-loop appears twice in its vertex’s order, its two ends adjacent, enclosing a face of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"length 1. Parallel copies sit side by side, each consecutive pair enclosing a face of length 2."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Each clockwise order starts at the first edge of "},{"code":"incidentEdges(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Faces.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The face after the half-edge from u along edge e to w continues with the half-edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"before e in the clockwise order at w, so a face lies to the right of each of its half-edges.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Faces are counted per connected component, and an isolated vertex has none: two disjoint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"triangles have four faces.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The embedding keeps the graph it was made from (copy-on-write, so O(1)); mutating the graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"afterwards does not change it. When a graph has several embeddings, which one is returned is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not specified, but it depends only on the graph’s rows: graphs with the same vertices, the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge positions and the same incidence order get the same embedding."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PlanarEmbedding"}],"symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:9Planarity15PlanarEmbeddingV","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PlanarEmbedding","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Planarity"}],"title":"PlanarEmbedding"},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Planarity\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/Planarity\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/Planarity\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/Planarity\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Planarity\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/ClockwiseIncidentEdges","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/ClockwiseNeighborIndices","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation